  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $4\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}>-{6}^{3x-2}-{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} & >-{6}^{3x-2}-{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} \\\\ 4\\cdot {6}^{3x-2}+{6}^{3x-2}+{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{3x-2} & >0 \\\\ (4+1+{x}^{2}){6}^{3x-2} & >0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+5){6}^{3x-2} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${6}^{3x-2}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+5){6}^{3x-2} & >0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+5 & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}^{2}+5>0$ for all values of $x,$ the solution is all real numbers.",
